    <span class="tg-timestamp">2026-11-03T08:34:10+08:00</span>

    <div class="tg-white-space-preserve white-space-preserve tg-msg"><a href="https://twitter.com/rikiyatakehi">Rikiya Takehi</a>:
We asked GPT-6 Astra to edit Qwen3.5-0.8B weights to improve math.
It directly changed only 0.016% of weights, fixing 0.8B's reasoning loops &amp; improving math up to 6x and even instruction following 3x, without gradients or training.

We call this Weight-Space Programming: frontier LLMs can now natively read/write neural network weights! 🧵
Blog: <a href="https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/">rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-sp…</a>

<a href="https://twitter.com/rikiyatakehi/status/2117313742891327994">https://twitter.com/rikiyatakehi/status/2117313742891327994</a></div>
